sses parsed-hostname equality to `paper-api.alpaca.markets` (alpaca_adapter.py:45-56). The safe Tier-2 run is structurally incapable of reaching a live port (actions.py:67-89).\\n- **Console-action audit is solid:** every safe/gated action writes a redacted, append-only `AuditEntry` (audit.py:29-70), with a defense-in-depth secret-redaction pass over the full surface (proc.py:48-63), honouring ADR-013 sec.6/sec.7.\\n\\n### Gaps (each tied to evidence)\\n- **No startup reconcile, no broker reads.** There is zero `GET /v2/positions` or `GET /v2/account`; the live path loads only local JSON and places a blind market BUY. This is a *governed* gap — ADR-014 sec.6 plans the mandatory reconcile-then-act — but it is the single most important pre-live item.\\n- **No Alpaca `client_order_id`** in the POST body (alpaca_adapter.py:142-144), so there is no broker-side 422 dedup behind the internal once-ever guard. Governed (ADR-014 sec.6).\\n- **Two latent input-fidelity defects in the guard request:** `daily_pnl` is all-time realized P&L, and `trades_today` is the all-time fill count (runtime.py:91,99), both fed to guards named 'daily'. The `trades_today` proxy fails *safe* (over-blocks after 10 lifetime fills); the `daily_pnl` proxy is simply wrong across day boundaries. Documented as v0 approximations, but incorrect as written.\\n- **The GLD-vs-gold-spot price defect** is confirmed live in `run_chain` (engine.py:95) -> `execute` -> Alpaca `slippage_bps` (alpaca_adapter.py:116-121): a $/oz spot price (~4624) is used as the $/share GLD fill reference, producing meaningless slippage and wrong P&L units. Dormant today, but a real latent bug; ADR-014 sec.5 elevates its fix (B6) to blocking.\\n- **No cash-cap/account check, no QUEUED/PARTIAL/EXECUTION_UNCERTAIN state machine, no FLAT->SELL exit** — all governed by ADR-014 sec.6 and all absent (synchronous binary fill; non-LONG refused, alpaca_adapter.py:106-113).\\n- **No operator kill switch.** `halt` is only a read-only OperationalInput field on the dashboard and a guard input; no ops action can set it. This one is *ungoverned* (no ADR mandates a runtime halt), though mitigated by the one-shot gated model + default-OFF adapter + unregister-schedule.\\n\\n### Bottom line\\nThe internal safety spine (idempotency, GATE-001 guards, gated-live enablement, console audit) is genuinely strong and correctly composed. Every reconciliation/broker-realism gap is a *deliberate, ADR-014-governed* boundary on a dormant adapter — none is an ungoverned omission except the (low-severity) absence of an explicit kill switch. The two things I would not ship live without fixing are real code-as-written defects: the gold-spot price/slippage reference and the mislabeled cumulative 'daily' guard inputs.###PART 1 §1 Concept Overview + §2 Technical Feasibility (key=concept)#{1}": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"sjvg7w","at":1782068239231},"key":"_audit_narr.txt##2.9 Reconciliation & safety + Operations Control Plane — audit\\n\\n**Framing.** el_nino is a single-instrument (GLD), paper-only, long-or-flat decision->execution pipeline whose only two Alpaca surfaces are default-OFF, fail-closed stdlib plugs. The Alpaca execution adapter is built-but-DORMANT (no LONG is emitted pre-calibration, ADR-012), so most reconciliation/safety gaps below are latent, not live failures. I classified each against the governing ADRs (ADR-013 ops control plane = accepted/active; ADR-014 operable adapter v1 = draft/not-started, hard-paused).\\n\\n### Strengths (verified)\\n- **Internal duplicate-order protection is real and layered.** `PortfolioState.has_execution(source_snapshot_id)` short-circuits a re-fill before `port.fill` (engine.py:91-92), and `RuntimeLedger.has_admit` does the same at admission (paper_runtime/predicates.py:31-35). Crash-consistency is deliberately reasoned: portfolio-first-then-ledger persistence (orchestration/runtime.py:9-12) makes a crash a safe redo, never a double-fill.\\n- **The GATE-001 guard battery is complete and correctly wired before execution.** All five hard-limit predicates (position size, daily loss cap, max trades, max positions, withdrawal-disabled) run as a short-circuit conjunction (predicates.py:66-72) via `run_guard` *before* `execute` on the live chain path (orchestration/engine.py:96-106), and a fill can only exist on an approved guard_result (models.py:303-305). `load_config_from_env` fails closed on any missing limit (guardrail_engine.py:43-47). The L3 cooldown guard (PRED-008) adds deterministic pacing.\\n- **The gated-live enablement matches ADR-013 to the letter.** The only route to a live Alpaca order — `run_chain_now_alpaca_paper` — enforces confirm modal + append-only audit + a *server-side* `adapter.client is None` precondition that refuses without placing an order (gated.py:84-90), and the client is non-None only when paper creds are present AND the URL passes parsed-hostname equality to `paper-api.alpaca.markets` (alpaca_adapter.py:45-56). The safe Tier-2 run is structurally incapable of reaching a live port (actions.py:67-89).\\n- **Console-action audit is solid:** every safe/gated action writes a redacted, append-only `AuditEntry` (audit.py:29-70), with a defense-in-depth secret-redaction pass over the full surface (proc.py:48-63), honouring ADR-013 sec.6/sec.7.\\n\\n### Gaps (each tied to evidence)\\n- **No startup reconcile, no broker reads.** There is zero `GET /v2/positions` or `GET /v2/account`; the live path loads only local JSON and places a blind market BUY. This is a *governed* gap — ADR-014 sec.6 plans the mandatory reconcile-then-act — but it is the single most important pre-live item.\\n- **No Alpaca `client_order_id`** in the POST body (alpaca_adapter.py:142-144), so there is no broker-side 422 dedup behind the internal once-ever guard. Governed (ADR-014 sec.6).\\n- **Two latent input-fidelity defects in the guard request:** `daily_pnl` is all-time realized P&L, and `trades_today` is the all-time fill count (runtime.py:91,99), both fed to guards named 'daily'. The `trades_today` proxy fails *safe* (over-blocks after 10 lifetime fills); the `daily_pnl` proxy is simply wrong across day boundaries. Documented as v0 approximations, but incorrect as written.\\n- **The GLD-vs-gold-spot price defect** is confirmed live in `run_chain` (engine.py:95) -> `execute` -> Alpaca `slippage_bps` (alpaca_adapter.py:116-121): a $/oz spot price (~4624) is used as the $/share GLD fill reference, producing meaningless slippage and wrong P&L units. Dormant today, but a real latent bug; ADR-014 sec.5 elevates its fix (B6) to blocking.\\n- **No cash-cap/account check, no QUEUED/PARTIAL/EXECUTION_UNCERTAIN state machine, no FLAT->SELL exit** — all governed by ADR-014 sec.6 and all absent (synchronous binary fill; non-LONG refused, alpaca_adapter.py:106-113).\\n- **No operator kill switch.** `halt` is only a read-only OperationalInput field on the dashboard and a guard input; no ops action can set it. This one is *ungoverned* (no ADR mandates a runtime halt), though mitigated by the one-shot gated model + default-OFF adapter + unregister-schedule.\\n\\n### Bottom line\\nThe internal safety spine (idempotency, GATE-001 guards, gated-live enablement, console audit) is genuinely strong and correctly composed. Every reconciliation/broker-realism gap is a *deliberate, ADR-014-governed* boundary on a dormant adapter — none is an ungoverned omission except the (low-severity) absence of an explicit kill switch. The two things I would not ship live without fixing are real code-as-written defects: the gold-spot price/slippage reference and the mislabeled cumulative 'daily' guard inputs.###PART 1 §1 Concept Overview + §2 Technical Feasibility (key=concept)#{1}","lines":[118,118],"size":11,"outlinks":[],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
